@{
    ViewBag.Title = "About";
}

<section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Our story</p>
        <h1>One cart, one obsession, one neighborhood</h1>
        <p class="page-hero-lede">Brew Haven started as a two-person espresso cart outside the Riverbend library. The coffee got better; the queue got longer; one day we had keys to a corner shop.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container split split-reverse">
        <div class="split-media reveal">
            <img src="@Url.Content("~/Content/images/interior.jpg")" alt="The Brew Haven cafe interior — warm light, wooden tables and the espresso bar" />
        </div>
        <div class="split-body">
            <p class="eyebrow">The shop on Willow Lane</p>
            <h2>Built for people who linger</h2>
            <p>When we found the Willow Lane space in 2021, the brief was simple: a room that feels like your kitchen if your kitchen had a $12,000 espresso machine. Forty-two seats, a window bench for laptop days, a big communal table nobody has to leave, and a bar low enough that you can watch your drink being made.</p>
            <p>We kept the cart, by the way. It still makes an appearance at the Saturday farmers market every summer — ask for "the usual" and one of the original baristas will know exactly what you mean.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-cream">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="stat-band">
            <div class="stat"><strong>2016</strong><span>founded as an espresso cart</span></div>
            <div class="stat"><strong>12</strong><span>single origins roasted a year</span></div>
            <div class="stat"><strong>42</strong><span>seats, and none of them rushed</span></div>
            <div class="stat"><strong>4:45am</strong><span>when the bakery ovens go on</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head center">
            <p class="eyebrow">What we believe</p>
            <h2>Four house rules we actually keep</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="tiles-4">
            <div class="tile reveal">
                <span class="tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21c-5-3.5-8-7-8-11a5 5 0 0 1 8-4 5 5 0 0 1 8 4c0 4-3 7.5-8 11z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path></svg></span>
                <h3>Pay farmers properly</h3>
                <p>We buy direct or through importers we've visited, and we publish what we pay per pound on the shop corkboard.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile reveal">
                <span class="tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 3v7a5 5 0 0 0 10 0V3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path><path d="M7 6h4M13 6h4M12 15v6M9 21h6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span>
                <h3>Make it here or not at all</h3>
                <p>Syrups, granola, salsa verde and every pastry are made in our kitchen. Nothing reheated from a box, ever.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile reveal">
                <span class="tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></rect><path d="M3 9h18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path><path d="M6.5 13.5h6M6.5 16h9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span>
                <h3>No laptop shaming</h3>
                <p>Buy one drink, stay four hours. The window bench has outlets; the music is quiet enough to think.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tile reveal">
                <span class="tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6c-6-1.5-13 1.5-13 9 0 1.5.3 2.8.9 3.9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path><path d="M20 6c1 5.5-2.5 10-8.5 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path><path d="M4.5 20c1.5-4 5-7.5 9.5-9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span>
                <h3>Lighten our footprint</h3>
                <p>Compostable cups by default, a discount for bring-your-own, and grounds go home with gardeners for free.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Milestones</p>
            <h2>From cart to corner shop</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="timeline">
            <li>
                <span class="tl-year">2016</span>
                <div class="tl-body"><h3>The cart outside the library</h3><p>Two borrowed grinders, a hand-painted sign and a line that taught us everything about pacing a morning rush.</p></div>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="tl-year">2018</span>
                <div class="tl-body"><h3>The bakery joins</h3><p>Jonas and his croissant laminator move in above the roastery; the 8am crowd stops asking whether we have food.</p></div>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="tl-year">2021</span>
                <div class="tl-body"><h3>Willow Lane opens</h3><p>Forty-two seats, a proper kitchen and the window bench that regularly books out by 9am on weekends.</p></div>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="tl-year">2024</span>
                <div class="tl-body"><h3>The roastery corner</h3><p>Our little roaster gets a window seat of its own — cuppings every first Saturday, open to anyone curious enough to slurp.</p></div>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head center">
            <p class="eyebrow">The people</p>
            <h2>Say hi to the folks behind the bar</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="team-grid">
            <div class="team-card reveal">
                <span class="avatar">AO</span>
                <h3>Amara Okafor</h3>
                <p class="role">Head roaster</p>
                <p>Chases washed Ethiopians the way other people chase weather fronts. Runs the first-Saturday cuppings.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="team-card reveal">
                <span class="avatar">JP</span>
                <h3>Jonas Petrov</h3>
                <p class="role">Head baker</p>
                <p>Owns the 4:45am alarm. Believes a croissant should audibly shatter, and will hand you a test batch to prove it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="team-card reveal">
                <span class="avatar">TS</span>
                <h3>Theo Silva</h3>
                <p class="role">Bar lead</p>
                <p>Dials in the espresso twice a day and remembers regulars' orders down to "extra hot, one sugar, no stirring".</p>
            </div>
            <div class="team-card reveal">
                <span class="avatar">MK</span>
                <h3>Min-ji Kang</h3>
                <p class="role">General manager</p>
                <p>Keeps the schedule, the corkboard and the compost program running. Writes the playlist on Fridays.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="center-cta"><a class="btn btn-outline" href="@Url.Action("Contact", "Home")">Work with us — say hello</a></p>
    </div>
</section>
